    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ageBand` derivation from an optional request `birthDate`, computed against `registrationDate`. I kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods.\n\n**Changes (6 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (date) to `OwnerFields` (request) and read-only `ageBand` (string) to `Owner` (response). Drives DTO generation; `birthDate` auto-maps in both directions by name.\n\n2. **`AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper class (mirroring `MembershipLevel`/`CheckDigit`) with a single static `of(Owner)`: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18) / `ADULT` (18\u201364) / `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when no `birthDate` so the field is simply absent. Zero surrounding complexity to hold.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line delegating `ageBand` to `AgeBand.of(owner)`. The interface method's complexity stays at 1; no logic added there.\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 a `birthDate` field plus a plain getter/setter (each CC 1), so persistence survives the POST\u2192GET round trip. No existing method touched.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` column (tests run on the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n6. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional owner seed inserts to match the new column.\n\nThe derivation lives entirely in the new `AgeBand` helper (no `WMC_other`), and every existing method I touched was either a trivial accessor or a single-line mapper addition \u2014 no method or class grew in complexity.\n\nThe test posts `birthDate: 1990-01-01`; against a `registrationDate` of 2026 that yields `ADULT`, which the GET response now returns.",
